title: Scale validator self-stake incentive by era-points performance
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    Validator self-stake incentive payout is now distributed proportionally across
    elected validators using the weighted-mean share
    `share_i = (w_i · ep_i) / Σ_j(w_j · ep_j)`, where `w_j` is each validator's
    per-era incentive weight and `ep_j` is their era points. The sum runs over
    every validator with non-zero era points. Validators with zero era points
    receive nothing, and their notional share is implicitly redistributed by the
    formula. The full era budget is paid out to non-zero performers, so there is no pot residue to forfeit.
crates:
- name: pallet-staking-async
  bump: minor
